    "updated_at": "2022-02-18T16:35:43Z",
    "body": "So if we can't resolve this quickly we should probably revert because having broken IDL in the spec is quite bad.\r\n\r\n@mysteryDate the question is what `roundRect(1, 2, 3, 4)` should do. In particular in JS we try to maintain the invariant that when you have a trailing dictionary argument, `roundRect(1, 2, 3, 4)` ~ `roundRect(1, 2, 3, 4, {})` which in this case, because of how DOMPointInit is defined, is ~ `roundRect(1, 2, 3, 4, { x: 0, y: 0 })`.\r\n\r\nIs that OK?\r\n\r\nIf so then this is easy to fix, and we can just change the argument to `optional (stuff) radii = 0` or `optional (stuff) radii = {}`.\r\n\r\nIf that is not OK then we have to break platform consistency in some tricky way that will work poorly with IDL.",
